    "segments": [
      {
        "role": "host",
        "speaker": "Host",
        "sourceStart": 6,
        "sourceEnd": 172,
        "text": "Welcome to Tech Talk. Today we're talking about privacy and how we form opinions. I'm joined by Dr. Chen, a researcher in digital ethics. Dr. Chen, thanks for coming.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "cd95eec364a87bcd14a06583fbfe158f2081aec9aa7dce6df6e1496657c835d1",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0
      },
      {
        "role": "dr chen",
        "speaker": "Dr. Chen",
        "sourceStart": 183,
        "sourceEnd": 204,
        "text": "Thanks for having me.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-ChristopherNeural",
        "textHash": "a613b2a7db2dc396e2b1d0b3b6463a44697d89e6dbc060c5e6916603e3b2cb0a",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "host",
        "speaker": "Host",
        "sourceStart": 211,
        "sourceEnd": 292,
        "text": "So, many people worry that their phones are listening to them. What do you think?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "0ca4f9dc45d7a1ce54fcedaa3fd17688d67b964bb4e65417b5a70f47532b5dd7",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "dr chen",
        "speaker": "Dr. Chen",
        "sourceStart": 303,
        "sourceEnd": 542,
        "text": "Well, it's true that our devices collect a lot of data. But the idea that they are secretly recording everything is mostly a myth. What actually happens is that apps track what you click and where you go. That data is used to show you ads.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-ChristopherNeural",
        "textHash": "a2fd12f036cc838b9843cdde91509b1bec8f06a6f594ff435f1d4956d778a690",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "host",
        "speaker": "Host",
        "sourceStart": 549,
        "sourceEnd": 630,
        "text": "But sometimes I talk about a product and then see an ad for it. Isn't that proof?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "ce2836c2a91b318b0cb2d4c8b25dc428ce14fd6f72ab72202d9d38a7f374897d",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "dr chen",
        "speaker": "Dr. Chen",
        "sourceStart": 641,
        "sourceEnd": 890,
        "text": "I understand why it feels like that. But it's usually coincidence, or the app knows your location and habits. For example, if you walk past a shop, your phone might record that. Then later, you see an ad for that shop. It's not because it heard you.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-ChristopherNeural",
        "textHash": "293894203fa36b42bc6d49f753e089eb01cee1b9e864f2e3d12183e05e220146",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "host",
        "speaker": "Host",
        "sourceStart": 897,
        "sourceEnd": 966,
        "text": "That's reassuring. So what should people do to protect their privacy?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "5b6267487ccb067b46d39de4d3c0b5e4c4f1f79eece58768eb77a126b72b7a33",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "dr chen",
        "speaker": "Dr. Chen",
        "sourceStart": 977,
        "sourceEnd": 1233,
        "text": "First, check your app permissions. Many apps ask for access to your microphone or contacts when they don't need it. You can turn those off. Second, use a strong password and two-factor authentication. Third, be careful about what you share on social media.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-ChristopherNeural",
        "textHash": "bede287edefa5a74112fd735e0724cfd7d93257b3573414d760a739ae2bc07ec",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "host",
        "speaker": "Host",
        "sourceStart": 1240,
        "sourceEnd": 1286,
        "text": "Some people say privacy is dead. Do you agree?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "eff66dd4cdc5d3bf2069ba8f7043554c8abdfb7c08ea956b87217e2a9be735a4",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "dr chen",
        "speaker": "Dr. Chen",
        "sourceStart": 1297,
        "sourceEnd": 1528,
        "text": "Not at all. I think privacy is not dead, but it is changing. We need to be more active in managing it. If we don't pay attention, companies will collect more data than we want. But if we take simple steps, we can keep some control.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-ChristopherNeural",
        "textHash": "3ef70d342adc08faabdb6cfe49814c1c838ad1e05bb35e4b58b347b182963697",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "host",
        "speaker": "Host",
        "sourceStart": 1535,
        "sourceEnd": 1590,
        "text": "What about young people? They seem to share everything.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "829817983d2ef654faa41f6a58d2f5a4d8b9386c9b6f968d6462d2f961345dd8",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "dr chen",
        "speaker": "Dr. Chen",
        "sourceStart": 1601,
        "sourceEnd": 1892,
        "text": "Actually, research shows that many young people care about privacy. They just have different ideas about what is private. For them, sharing photos with friends is normal, but they don't want companies to track them. So it's not that they don't care; it's that they have different priorities.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-ChristopherNeural",
        "textHash": "ec08e8ca7769d6ae5a853d27a51f42805e1c5df593305a33f62ab8d31aec8bf8",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "host",
        "speaker": "Host",
        "sourceStart": 1899,
        "sourceEnd": 1977,
        "text": "Interesting. So what's the most important thing our listeners should remember?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "f52bd1b1bf683a35a0f359d8ac43001e26ce977e22df9b2756fa5bbfea796efa",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "dr chen",
        "speaker": "Dr. Chen",
        "sourceStart": 1988,
        "sourceEnd": 2146,
        "text": "I think the key is to be aware. Don't assume that you have no control. You do have choices. And it's okay to say no to apps that ask for too much information.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-ChristopherNeural",
        "textHash": "da48e7ab498ead6d8e67bf34d5d60609f6cff52b79ed0dd27343bf314e6ec472",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "host",
        "speaker": "Host",
        "sourceStart": 2153,
        "sourceEnd": 2187,
        "text": "Great advice. Thank you, Dr. Chen.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "2269fc61133b87914fd14885fc3fa6e5ddcb6c20ae25ba75ef7a734495772ef3",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "dr chen",
        "speaker": "Dr. Chen",
        "sourceStart": 2198,
        "sourceEnd": 2210,
        "text": "My pleasure.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-ChristopherNeural",
        "textHash": "c4a93eaaa5a80f6820bfefd0aa85ba20402b532c89f2635760c00d7e7871215e",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      }
    ]
  },
